  ('1113379079426454923', 'Bolek and Lolek in the Wild West', 1986, 'Animation, Family, Adventure, Western', 'Ryszard Biesok, Stanisław Dülz, Józef Byrdy', 'Andrzej Orzechowski, Adam Hajduk, Leszek Mech', 'Ilona Kuśmierska-Kocyłak, Danuta Przesmycka, Piotr Fronczewski, Janusz Rewiński, Andrzej Gawroński, Krzysztof Krupiński, Dorota Lanton, Henryk Łapiński', null, 'The dangerous thug Pif-Paf escapes from prison. Bolek and Lolek bravely chase after him through the prairie, canyons and rocky mountains.', 'The dangerous thug Pif-Paf escapes from prison. Bolek and Lolek bravely chase after him through the prairie, canyons and rocky mountains.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/sOWNEPwulyL9h1PTB44r5Uwli7F.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:59442'),
  ('506212661473816932', 'Bolero', 1934, 'Drama', 'Wesley Ruggles, Leo Tover', 'Horace Jackson', 'George Raft, Carole Lombard, Sally Rand, Frances Drake, William Frawley, Gertrude Michael, Ray Milland, Gloria Shea', 'NR', 'The complicated relationship between an ambitious, ruthless nightclub dancer and the woman he loves.', 'The complicated relationship between an ambitious, ruthless nightclub dancer and the woman he loves.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/cny4vyqPkCE93DbjcHGdn0RKJR8.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:188457'),
  ('163463911072084053', 'Bolero', 1981, 'Drama, Music', 'Claude Lelouch, Jean Boffety', 'Claude Lelouch', 'Robert Hossein, Nicole Garcia, Geraldine Chaplin, Daniel Olbrychski, Jorge Donn, Rita Poelvoorde, Macha Méril, Évelyne Bouix', null, 'The film follows four families, with different nationalities (French, German, Russian and American) but with the same passion for music, from the 1930s to the 1960s. The various story lines cross each other time and again in different places and times, with their own theme scores that evolve as time passes. The main event in the film is the Second World War, which throws the stories of the four musical families together and mixes their fates. Although all characters are fictional, many of them are loosely based on historical musical icons (Édith Piaf, Josephine Baker, Herbert von Karajan, Glenn Miller, Rudolf Nureyev, etc.) The Boléro dance sequence at the end brings all the threads together.', 'The film follows four families, with different nationalities (French, German, Russian and American) but with the same passion for music, from the 1930s to the 1960s. The various story lines cross each other time and again in different places and times, with their own theme scores that evolve as time passes. The main event in the film is the Second World War, which throws the stories of the four musical families together and mixes their fates. Although all characters are fictional, many of them are loosely based on historical musical icons (Édith Piaf, Josephine Baker, Herbert von Karajan, Glenn Miller, Rudolf Nureyev, etc.) The Boléro dance sequence at the end brings all the threads together.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/6FUXOIU9pa835mNRD4bG4MKzdrx.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:37335'),
  ('219985930444262545', 'Bolero', 1984, 'Drama, Romance', 'John Derek, John Derek', 'John Derek', 'Bo Derek, Andrea Occhipinti, Ana Obregón, Ian Cochrane, Mirta Miller, George Kennedy, Olivia D''Abo, Greg Bensen', 'R', 'Follows the tale of a young woman’s sexual awakening and subsequent journey around the world in pursuit of her ideal lover. Encounters include an Arabian sheik and a Spanish bullfighter. Her friend and butler accompany her and help to arrange her couplings.', 'Follows the tale of a young woman’s sexual awakening and subsequent journey around the world in pursuit of her ideal lover. Encounters include an Arabian sheik and a Spanish bullfighter. Her friend and butler accompany her and help to arrange her couplings.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/pQNjzG51FB9ngy8pi2HVELeFEkS.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:5896'),
  ('109659364374734392', 'Boléro', 2024, 'Drama', 'Nans Laborde-Jourdàa, Manuel Bolaños, Leia Hasrouty', 'Nans Laborde-Jourdàa', 'François Chaignaud, Muriel Laborde-Jourdàa, Mellie Laborde-Jourdàa, Roger Marcillaud, Loïc M''Bora, Yan Jumbou', null, 'Fran is in his hometown to rest and visit his mother. Following the jerky rhythm of Bolero, this journey along the paths of memory and desire will lead him and the whole village to a joyfully chaotic climax.', 'Fran is in his hometown to rest and visit his mother. Following the jerky rhythm of Bolero, this journey along the paths of memory and desire will lead him and the whole village to a joyfully chaotic climax.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/afDqfDoG02kDEvdLYxQZX58VlHM.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:1116569'),
